- 𠂇 (piě) - person-like
- 𢛳 (xīn) - heart (variant)
CLASSROOM EXAMPLE SENTENCES
- 上课的时候，不可以说英文。 - During class, you cannot speak English.
- 你最近看了什么新闻？ - What news have you read recently?
- 你可以送我回家吗？ - Can you take me home?
- 你抽过烟吗？ - Have you ever smoked?
- 我会骑自行车。 - I can ride a bike.
- 我能跑十公里。 - I can run ten kilometers.
- 火车站离医院很近。 - The train station is very close to the hospital.
- 我陪妈妈去医院。 - I accompanied my mother to the hospital.
- 你学了多长时间中文了？ - How long have you been studying Chinese?
- 你叫什么名字？ - What is your name?
- 他是我的老师。 - He is my teacher.
- 我认识他。 - I know him.
- 你今天几点上班？ - What time do you go to work today?
- 我还在学习。 - I am still studying.
- 这件事很重要。 - This matter is very important.
- 你现在怎么样？ - How are you doing now?
- 我想先吃饭，然后再去。 - I want to eat first, then go.
- 回去以后我还要打电话。 - After I go back, I still need to make a phone call.
- 谁想试一试说一个句子？ - Who wants to try saying a sentence?
- 这个孩子三岁多了。 - This child is a little over three years old.
- 他等了两个多小时。 - He waited for more than two hours.
- 我有几个中国同事。 - I have a few Chinese colleagues.
- 她在附近吗？ - Is she nearby?
- 你为什么戴眼镜？ - Why are you wearing glasses?
- 你学了多长时间中文了？ - How long have you been studying Chinese?
- 我不喜欢中文，我讨厌。 - I don't like Chinese, I hate it.
- 你穿了多长时间了？ - How long have you been wearing this?
- 如果你要坐飞机，你应该很早到机场。 - If you are taking a plane, you should get to the airport very early.
- 我不同意我的同学。 - I disagree with my classmate.
- 他以前在医院工作。 - He used to work at the hospital.
- 这里有好几家四川饭馆。 - There are quite a few Sichuan restaurants here.
- 我好饿啊，我们找个饭馆吃饭吧。 - I am so hungry, let’s find a restaurant to eat.
- 我生病了。 - I am sick.
- 我太累了，想休息几天。 - I am too tired, I want to rest for a few days.
- 他骑自行车去上班。 - He rides his bike to work.
- 明天是她的生日，你想送她什么？ - Tomorrow is her birthday, what would you like to give her?
- 这本书要几百块钱。 - This book costs several hundred yuan.
- 他想买几个蛋糕。 - He wants to buy a few cakes.
- 老师是中国人。 - The teacher is Chinese.
- 现在我在公司。 - I am at the company now.
- 我的姐姐有两个孩子。 - My older sister has two children.
- 这个多少钱？ - How much is this?
- 我每天七点起床。 - I get up at seven every day.
- 我打算明年去中国。 - I plan to go to China next year.
- 泰国菜又便宜又好吃。 - Thai food is both cheap and delicious.
- 你的英语说得真好！ - You speak English so well!
- 你先一直往前走，再往左转。 - First go straight ahead, then turn left.
- 我可以加你的微信吗？ - Can I add your WeChat?
- 对不起，请问厕所在哪里？ - Excuse me, may I ask where the restroom is?
- 今天晚上我们去酒吧吧。 - Let’s go to the bar tonight.
- 他不但每天运动，而且吃很少的饭。 - He not only exercises every day but also eats very little.
- 你一定要试一下这个菜。 - You definitely must try this dish.
- 我从来没有想过这个问题。 - I have never thought about this question.
- 祝你快乐 - I hope you are happy every day
- 这本书要几百块钱。 - This book costs several hundred yuan.
- 他们买了几十张票。 - They bought a few dozen tickets.
- 他三十多岁。 - He is over 30 years old.
- 他三十几岁。 - He is over 30 years old.
- 我听了二十多遍这个故事。 - I’ve heard this story more than 20 times.
- 我听了二十几遍这个故事。 - I’ve heard this story more than 20 times.
- 我已经吃饭了。 - I have already eaten.
- 她已经回家了。 - She has already gone home.
- 她已经结婚了。 - She’s already married.
- 他学习中文已经三年了。 - He has been studying Chinese for three years already.
- 几百个汉字 - A few hundred Chinese characters
- 别吃太多蛋糕了！ - Don’t eat too much cake!
- 现在我给大家分享我的屏幕。 - Now I am going to share my screen with everyone.
- 你要选哪？ - Which one are you going to choose?
- 请你选择一个。 - Please choose one.
- 你怎么看？ - What do you think?
- 请你读。 - Please read.
- 和中国人一样的。 - Just like a Chinese person.
- 我可以第一个。 - I can be the first.
- 读这些词。 - Read these words.
- 两个人刚认识。 - Two people just met each other.
- 谁想试一试说一个句子？ - Who wants to try saying a sentence?
- 大家知道吗？ - Does everyone know?
- 如果是这样的蛋糕…… - If it’s this kind of cake…
- 你们觉得蛋糕太甜了吗？ - Do you think the cake is too sweet?
- 你有没有买票？ - Did you buy a ticket?
- 请大家用中文说一说谁是阿姨？ - Please everyone say in Chinese who the auntie is.
- 请一个同学用中文说一说同事是谁？ - Please ask a classmate to say in Chinese who a coworker is.
- 那你介绍你的猫！ - Then introduce your cat!
- 大家明白了吗？ - Does everyone understand?
- 同意吗？ - Do you agree?
- 谁结婚了？ - Who got married?
- 你结婚结得早吗？ - Did you get married early?
- 我是一个宝宝。 - I am a baby.
- 我搬过大概5次家。 - I’ve moved about five times.
- 你最好的朋友结婚了吗？ - Did your best friend get married?
- 你最好的朋友和谁结婚了？ - Who did your best friend marry?
- 我想再搬家。 - I want to move again.
- 因为中国非常棒。 - Because China is amazing.
- 我回家的时候，我的丈夫正在准备晚饭。 - When I get home, my husband is preparing dinner.
- 你准备好了吗？ - Are you ready?
- 准备好了。 - Ready / I am ready.
- 我希望说中文说得很流利。 - I hope to speak Chinese very fluently.
- 我小的时候，希望是运动员，但是现在我不是。 - When I was little, I wanted to be an athlete, but now I’m not.
- 高铁比火车快。 - A high-speed train is faster than a regular train.
- 高铁比火车更快。 - A high-speed train is faster than a regular train.
- 高铁比火车快,飞机比高铁更快。 - A high-speed train is faster than a regular train, an airplane is even faster than a high-speed train.
- 飞机比火车快得多。 - An airplane is much faster than a train.
- 飞机比火车快多了。 - An airplane is much faster than a train.
- 今天比昨天热一点儿。 - Today is a bit hotter than yesterday.
- 昨天没有今天热。 - Yesterday was not as hot as today.
- 虾比牛肉贵四块钱。 - Shrimp is 4 yuan more expensive than beef.
- 大人没有孩子快乐。 - Adults are not as happy as kids.
- 蓝色的衣服比黑色的衣服贵得多。 - The blue clothes are much more expensive than the black clothes.
- 蓝色的衣服比黑色的衣服小一点儿。 - The blue clothes are a bit smaller than the black clothes.
- 蓝色的衣服比黑色的衣服更有名。 - The blue clothes are more famous than the black clothes.
- 蓝色的衣服没有黑色的衣服容易洗。 - The blue clothes are not as easy to wash as the black clothes.
- 我想买黑色的衣服因为蓝色的衣服比黑色的衣服便宜一点儿。 - I want to buy the black clothes because the blue clothes are a little cheaper than the black clothes.
- 这个西瓜又大又甜。 - This watermelon is big and sweet.
- 你想吃西瓜吗？ - Do you want to eat watermelon?
- 我给你买了一个生日蛋糕。 - I bought you a birthday cake.
- 我在网上买电影票吧。 - Let me buy movie tickets online.
- 请问我要去哪里买车票？ - Excuse me, where can I buy a bus ticket?
- 她的阿姨是工程师。 - Her aunt is an engineer.
- 你阿姨叫你。 - Your aunt is asking for you.
- 我的同事不都是中国人。 - Not all my colleagues are Chinese.
- 我不太喜欢和同事聊天。 - I don’t like chatting with colleagues much.
- 我们班有两个新同学。 - We have two new classmates in our class.
- 我们班只有一个女同学。 - We only have one female classmate in our class.
- 他跟一个律师结婚了。 - He married a lawyer.
- 小王去年刚结婚。 - Xiao Wang just got married last year.
- 我报名了老师的课。 - I signed up for the teacher’s class.
- 我们一起去报名吧。 - Let’s go sign up together.
- 我不常搬家。 - I don’t move often.
- 他从北京搬到了上海。 - He moved from Beijing to Shanghai.
- 电影什么时候开始？ - When does the movie start?
- 我每天早上八点开始工作。 - I start working at 8 AM every day.
- 我家在中国北方。 - My home is in northern China.
- 北方人说“一点儿”，南方人说“一点”。 - Northern people say “a little(r),” southern people say “a little.”
- 我没有去过中国西部。 - I have not been to western China.
- 现在是美国东部时间下午五点。 - Now it’s 5 PM Eastern Time in the USA.
- 你可以再说一遍吗？ - Can you say it again?
- 这本书非常好看，我看了两遍！ - This book is very interesting; I’ve read it twice!
- 老师，请你讲一讲怎么用“遍”。 - Teacher, please explain how to use “biàn.”
- 我不会讲上海话。 - I can’t speak Shanghainese.
- 这个孩子想再听一遍“西瓜的故事”。 - This child wants to hear the “watermelon story” again.
- 我给你讲一个故事吧。 - Let me tell you a story.
- 火车站怎么去？ - Excuse me, how do I get to the train station?
- 火车站和我的家不太远。 - The train station is not too far from my home.
- 我每天骑自行车去工作。 - I ride a bicycle to work every day.
- 这个城市有很多人骑自行车。 - There are many people riding bicycles in this city.
- 我没有坐过船。 - I have never taken a boat.
- 在曼谷，有的人每天坐船去公司。 - In Bangkok, some people take a boat to work every day.
- 中国的公共汽车又便宜又方便。 - Chinese buses are both cheap and convenient.
- 我不常坐公共汽车。 - I don’t often take the bus.
- 我很想试一试中国的高铁。 - I really want to try China’s high-speed rail.
- 请你告诉我怎么买高铁票？ - Please tell me how to buy a high-speed rail ticket?
- 昨天下雪了。 - It snowed yesterday.
- 我住的城市从来不下雪。 - The city where I live never snows.
- 下雨了，你等一下再出去吧。 - It’s raining. Wait a moment before going out.
- 已经下了三天雨了。 - It has already been raining for three days.
- 今天是晴天，所以很多人出去玩。 - Today is a sunny day, so many people are going out to have fun.
- 他们结婚的时候是一个大晴天。 - It was a bright sunny day when they got married.
- 今天是阴天，但是没有下雨。 - Today is a cloudy day, but it didn’t rain.
- 他最喜欢阴天，我真不知道为什么！ - He likes cloudy days the most. I really don’t know why!
- 今天特别冷！ - Today is especially cold!
- 我不喜欢冷的天气。 - I don’t like cold weather.
- 泰国每天都很热。 - Thailand is hot every day.
- 热死了！ - It’s insanely hot!
- 我准备回家了。 - I’m getting ready to go home.
- 我们明天开始上课，你准备好了吗？ - We start class tomorrow. Are you ready?
- 我下个星期搬家，希望不会下雨！ - I’m moving next week. I hope it won’t rain!
- 我希望三十多岁的时候可以有自己的公司。 - I hope to have my own company when I am in my thirties.
- 他还没有准备考试。 - He hasn’t prepared for the exam yet.
- 我没有考过汉语考试。 - I have never taken a Chinese exam.
- 我觉得汉字很容易。 - I think Chinese characters are very easy.
- 从北方搬到南方不是一件容易的事！ - Moving from the north to the south is not an easy thing!
- 我觉得骑自行车很难！ - I think riding a bicycle is very difficult!
- 这次考试不太难。 - This exam is not too difficult.
- 如果你快乐，我就快乐。 - If you’re happy, then I’m happy.
- 我希望我的女儿每天都快乐。 - I hope my daughter is happy every day.
- 她在附近吗？ (tā zài fùjìn ma?) - Is she nearby?
- 你为什么戴眼镜？ (nǐ wèishéme dài yǎnjìng?) - Why are you wearing glasses?
- 你学了多长时间中文了？ (nǐ xué le duō cháng shíjiān zhōngwén le?) - How long have you been studying Chinese?
- 我不喜欢中文，我讨厌。 (wǒ bù xǐhuān zhōngwén, wǒ tǎoyàn.) - I don’t like Chinese, I hate it.
- 你穿了多长时间了？ (nǐ chuān le duō cháng shíjiān le?) - How long have you been wearing this?
- 如果你要坐飞机，你应该很早到机场。 (rúguǒ nǐ yào zuò fēijī, nǐ yīnggāi hěn zǎo dào jīchǎng.) - If you are taking a plane, you should get to the airport very early.
- 飞机又比高铁便宜，又比高铁快。 (fēijī yòu bǐ gāotiě piányí, yòu bǐ gāotiě kuài.) - The plane is both cheaper and faster than the high-speed train.
- 我不同意我的同学。 (wǒ bù tóngyì wǒ de tóngxué.) - I disagree with my classmate.
- 她想去别的中文的地方。 (tā xiǎng qù bié de zhōngwén de dìfāng.) - She wants to go to other Chinese-speaking places.
- 讲故事比听故事更累。 (jiǎng gùshì bǐ tīng gùshì gèng lèi.) - Telling stories is more tiring than listening to stories.
- 猫没有狗让人快乐。 (māo méiyǒu gǒu ràng rén kuàilè.) - Cats are not as fun as dogs for people.
- 咖啡比茶味道好。 (kāfēi bǐ chá wèidào hǎo.) - Coffee tastes better than tea.
- 请问，最近的医院在哪里？ (qǐngwèn, zuìjìn de yīyuàn zài nǎlǐ?) - Excuse me, where is the nearest hospital?
- 他以前在医院工作。 (tā yǐqián zài yīyuàn gōngzuò.) - He used to work at the hospital.
- 这里有好几家四川饭馆。 (zhèlǐ yǒu hǎo jǐ jiā Sìchuān fànguǎn.) - There are quite a few Sichuan restaurants here.
- 我好饿啊，我们找个饭馆吃饭吧。 (wǒ hǎo è a, wǒmen zhǎo gè fànguǎn chīfàn ba.) - I am so hungry, let’s find a restaurant to eat.
- 老板办公室在前边。 (lǎobǎn bàngōngshì zài qiánbian.) - The boss’s office is ahead.
- 我们的办公室又大又漂亮。 (wǒmen de bàngōngshì yòu dà yòu piàoliang.) - Our office is big and beautiful.
- 他正在厨房准备晚饭呢。 (tā zhèngzài chúfáng zhǔnbèi wǎnfàn ne.) - He is currently preparing dinner in the kitchen.
- 厨房里有一个冰箱。 (chúfáng lǐ yǒu yī gè bīngxiāng.) - There is a refrigerator in the kitchen.
- 这个卧室比那个小一点儿。 (zhège wòshì bǐ nàgè xiǎo yīdiǎnr.) - This bedroom is a little smaller than that one.
- 我的新家只有一个卧室。 (wǒ de xīnjiā zhǐ yǒu yī gè wòshì.) - My new house only has one bedroom.
- 我生病了。 (wǒ shēngbìng le.) - I am sick.
- 他生病了，昨天没有来办公室。 (tā shēngbìng le, zuótiān méiyǒu lái bàngōngshì.) - He got sick and didn’t come to the office yesterday.
- 我太累了，想休息几天。 (wǒ tài lèi le, xiǎng xiūxi jǐ tiān.) - I am too tired, I want to rest for a few days.
- 现在我们先休息五分钟。 (xiànzài wǒmen xiān xiūxi wǔ fēnzhōng.) - Now let’s rest for five minutes.
- 在中国，很多人抽烟。 (zài Zhōngguó, hěn duō rén chōu yān.) - In China, many people smoke.
- 在高铁上不可以抽烟。 (zài gāotiě shàng bù kěyǐ chōu yān.) - You cannot smoke on the high-speed train.
- 他骑自行车去上班。 (tā qí zìxíngchē qù shàngbān.) - He rides his bike to work.
- 你什么时候下班？ (nǐ shénme shíhòu xiàbān?) - When do you get off work?
- 明天是她的生日，你想送她什么？ (míngtiān shì tā de shēngrì, nǐ xiǎng sòng tā shénme?) - Tomorrow is her birthday, what would you like to give her?
- 谢谢你送我回家。 (xièxiè nǐ sòng wǒ huí jiā.) - Thank you for sending me home.
- 别忘了吃药。 (bié wàngle chī yào.) - Don’t forget to take the medicine.
- 吃药以前要先吃饭。 (chī yào yǐqián yào xiān chī fàn.) - You must eat food before taking the medicine.
- 中国的公共汽车一般都很便宜。 (zhōngguó de gōnggòng qìchē yībān dōu hěn piányi.) - Public buses in China are generally very cheap.
- 这个城市一般不下雪。 (zhège chéngshì yībān bú xià xuě.) - It generally doesn’t snow in this city.
- 我们去别的地方看看吧。 (wǒmen qù biéde dìfang kàn kan ba.) - Let’s go to another place and take a look.
- 大家还有别的问题吗？ (dàjiā hái yǒu biéde de wèntí ma?) - Does anyone have any other questions?
- 我告诉你，你别告诉别人！ (wǒ gàosu nǐ, nǐ bié gàosu biéren!) - I’ll tell you, don’t tell other people!
- 今天我没空，你找别人吧。 (jīntiān wǒ méi kòng, nǐ zhǎo biéren ba.) - I don’t have time today, you can find someone else.
- 纽约在美国东北部。 - New York is in the northeastern United States.
- 今天纽约是阴天。 - It is overcast in New York today.
- 他想买几个蛋糕。 - He wants to buy a few cakes.
- 你每天怎么去上班？ - How do you go to work every day?
- 你生了什么病？ - What illness do you have?
- 你在离明年的中国新年还有一个月，你可以剪头发。 - There is one month until next Chinese New Year, so you can get a haircut.- A: 这个电影好看吗? B: 一般。 - A: Is this movie good? B: It’s so-so.
- 一辆自行车。 - one bicycle
- 不但...而且... - not only...but also...
- 中国的公共汽车一般都很便宜。 - Public buses in China are generally very cheap.
- 今天我没空,你找别人吧。 - I don’t have time today, you can find someone else.
- 他正在厨房准备晚饭呢。 - He is currently preparing dinner in the kitchen.
- 他生病了,昨天没有来办公室。 - He got sick and didn’t come to the office yesterday.
- 你上次帮朋友做了什么？ - What did you do to help a friend last time?
- 你什么时候下班? - When do you get off work?
- 你在离明年的中国新年还有是一个月，你可以剪头发。 - There is one month left before next year's Chinese New Year, so you can get a haircut.
- 你最不喜欢你的太太的什么？ - What do you dislike most about your wife?
- 你每天什么去上班？ - What time do you go to work every day?
- 你的卧室是什么颜色的？ - What color is your bedroom?
- 你的生日比我的生日早三个月。 - Your birthday is three months earlier than mine.
- 别人都会，为什么你不会？ - Everyone else knows how to do it, why don’t you know?
- 别忘了吃药。 - Don’t forget to take the medicine.
- 厨房里有一个冰箱。 - There is a refrigerator in the kitchen.
- 又...又... - ... as well as ... (又便宜又好吃。)
- 吃药以前要先吃饭。 - You must eat food before taking the medicine.
- 和比你大得多的人一起吃饭时，你不能比他先吃。 - When eating with someone much older than you, you cannot eat before him.
- 咖啡比茶味道好。 - Coffee tastes better than tea.
- 喝酒以后不能吃这个药。 - You can’t take this medicine after drinking alcohol.
- 因为今天下雨了堵车，所以我迟到了。 - Because it rained today and there was traffic, I was late.
- 在中国,很多人抽烟。 - In China, many people smoke.
- 在高铁上不可以抽烟。 - You cannot smoke on the high-speed train.
- 外面下大雨了，我们不能出去。 - It’s raining heavily, so we can’t go out.
- 大家还有别的问题吗? - Does anyone have any other questions?
- 她想去别的中文的地方。 - She wants to go to other Chinese-speaking places.
- 如果你吃太多甜的东西，你会牙疼。 - If you eat too many sweets, your teeth hurt.
- 如果你早上不喝咖啡，你的头会疼。 - If you don’t drink coffee in the morning, your head will hurt.
- 如果你跑得太快了，你会脚疼。 - If you run too fast, your feet hurt.
- 如果是这样的蛋糕... - If it’s this kind of cake...
- 已经...了 - to emphasize that something has already happened
- 师傅，麻烦你别抽烟。 - Master / Uncle, please don’t smoke.
- 怎么办？ - What should I do?
- 我从来没有抽过烟。 - I have never smoked.
- 我们去别的地方看看吧。 - Let’s go to another place and take a look.
- 我们店的衣服一般不可以换。 - Clothes in our store usually can’t be exchanged.
- 我们的办公室又大又漂亮。 - Our office is big and beautiful.
- 我会讲普通话。 - I can speak Mandarin.
- 我只学了三个月中文，就能和中国人聊天了。 - I only studied Chinese for three months, and I was already able to chat with Chinese people.
- 我告诉你,你别告诉别人! - I’ll tell you, don’t tell other people!
- 我回家的时候,我的丈夫正在准备晚饭 - When I get home, my husband is preparing dinner.
- 我在上班，我不可以接电话。 - I’m at work, so I can’t take calls.
- 我太累了,想休息几天。 - I am too tired, I want to rest for a few days.
- 我好饿啊,我们找个饭馆吃饭吧。 - I am so hungry, let’s find a restaurant to eat.
- 我家的附近有一个包子的饭馆。 - Near my home there is a steamed-bun restaurant.
- 我生病了，不能去上课。 - I’m sick, so I can’t go to class.
- 我的厨房离卧室有点儿远。 - My kitchen is a bit far from my bedroom.
- 我的家离纽约不远。 - My home is not far from New York.
- 我的新家只有一个卧室。 - My new house only has one bedroom.
- 我结婚结得早。 - I got married early.
- 我能喝十瓶啤酒。 - I can drink 10 bottles of beer.
- 我还没开始准备。 - I haven’t started preparing yet.
- 找一找这些词的图片。 - Look for pictures of these words.
- 明天是她的生日,你想送她什么? - Tomorrow is her birthday, what would you like to give her?
- 猫没有狗让人快乐。 - Cats are not as fun as dogs for people.
- 现在我们先休息五分钟。 - Now let’s rest for five minutes.
- 现在我们看一看这里有三个人（阿姨，同事，同学），请你选词，一个人来介绍。 - Now let’s look: here there are three people (auntie, coworker, classmate), please choose the word and let one person introduce.
- 现在离下课的时候八分钟。 - It is eight minutes before class ends.
- 看电影的时候，你喜欢坐在前面还是后面？ - When watching a movie, do you like to sit in the front or in the back?
- 离新年还有一个多月。 - There is still more than a month until the New Year.
- 离考试只有三天了！ - There are only three days left until the exam!
- 第一张图片是火车。 - The first picture is a train.
- 老板办公室在前边。 - The boss’s office is ahead.
- 讲故事比听故事更累。 - Telling stories is more tiring than listening to stories.
- 请问,最近的医院在哪里? - Excuse me, where is the nearest hospital?
- 请问，火车站怎么去？ - Excuse me, how do I get to the train station?
- 谁想试一试说一个句子? - Who wants to try saying a sentence?
- 谢谢你的帮助。 - Thank you for your help.
- 谢谢你送我回家。 - Thank you for sending me home.
- 还要别的吗？ - Anything else?
- 这个卧室比那个小一点儿。 - This bedroom is a little smaller than that one.
- 这个城市一般不下雪。 - It generally doesn’t snow in this city.
- 这儿离最近的饭馆大概三百米。 - This place is about 300 meters from the nearest restaurant.
- 这里不能抽烟。 - Smoking is not allowed here.
- 那现在我想请一个同学用蛋糕问一个问题。 - So now I want to ask a classmate to ask a question using cake.
- 飞机又比高铁便宜，又比高铁快。 - The plane is both cheaper and faster than the high-speed train.
- 饭馆比饭店小。 - Restaurants are smaller than hotels.
